lisa-design:
Round 2 (design §13, owner e2e feedback) — supersedes the round-1 notes about the drawer:
- R70: the structured editor drawer (AgentConfigEditorDrawer + OverlayFormEditor/PluginCard/FlagsSection/PoliciesSection/PolicyBundleCard/BundleFileList/New/CustomizeBundleDialog/EditorBanner/OverlayYamlEditor) is REMOVED. Do not reintroduce a form drawer; raw edits go through workspace/RawOverlayDialog (YAML, Apply → draft).
- R69 draft: ONE DraftState per agent in composables/agent-config/draftRegistry (module-level Map, in memory = browser session; no sessionStorage on purpose: a reload starts clean, beforeunload guards it). Both views bind to it via useConfigWorkspace(agentId, api, state). syncDraftState adopts a newer desired revision only while the draft is clean; a dirty draft keeps its base revision and meets the 409 flow on save (deliberate rebase, never silent).
- useOverlayDraft no longer has YAML mode (setMode/yamlText/flushYaml/hasUnsavedChanges removed); the raw dialog parses/coerces itself. "N pending changes" = changedLeafPaths(original, overlay) (arrays are one leaf). revertPointer(ptr) is the per-field undo (restores the saved overlay's value or absence).
- Workspace = provide/inject (WORKSPACE_KEY + the existing OVERLAY_DRAFT/EDITOR_CONTEXT/EDITOR_PERMISSIONS keys so useEditor/useBundleOps/PolicySourcesEditor/KeyValueEditor keep working). Components that inject must be CHILDREN of the component calling useConfigWorkspace (hence AgentPoliciesView → PoliciesWorkspace split).
- Placeholder base = the instance selected in the tab (state.selectedInstance) when loaded, else the first loaded detail. Instance details for every reported instance load in the background for editors only (after the selected instance's own load, so it is not fetched twice); readers never trigger it on the tab. The Policies view loads them for everyone (vendor file lists are read data).
- canEditPointer: forbidden pointers never; configure → everything else; configure-policy → /policy_bundles/** and /plugins/*/policies only. Review & save is disabled with saveDisabledReason (isPolicyOnlyChange over the previewed validated bases, else validationInstanceIds) — same rule as round 1, now on the shared bar.
- R71 states come from utils/agent-config/field-access (pure): forbidden = api/daemon/remote_config; restricted = fresh apply_safe instances with a reported remote_config whose trusted_sources / overridable_config_flags / allow_inline_policies would not apply a change there (mirrors agentconfig.Classify; value-dependent rules like already-used sources are left to the preview). Report/off-mode instances are NOT listed per field (InstanceModeNotice covers them).
- R62 vendor digest choice (policy-files.vendorArtifactFor): inline:<name>.extends.artifactDigest ONLY when that report's extends.source equals the draft's extends; else the artifact-digest of a report whose source IS the extends source; else a miss (no-report / no-digest / extends-mismatch) → confirm → module template. Reports are tried placeholder instance first, then every loaded instance. Artifact lists/files are cached per session (content-addressed). When a report has no file list (truncated) but a digest, the list comes from GET …/files.
- R64 template (utils/agent-config/rego-template.moduleTemplate) is VALID Rego with "TODO: …" placeholders and a `false` violation body (spec shows "…"; a literal `{ … }` body would not parse, so an untouched template would block the save). It passes the client contract hints as written. "Add file" (.rego) and "create from scratch" use it too; regoSkeleton is gone.
- R63 client hints (utils/agent-config/contract-hints) are line-based, column-1 rule heads only, never blocking; API PolicyErrors win: a hint with the same code+row as an API error is not shown twice. Markers prefix the code: "[missing-title] …".
- R66 swap-by-default lives in useBundleOps.assign(plugin, name, 'replace'|'alongside'); unassign of a swapped bundle puts the extended source back at the same index (inverse R22 swap) rather than dropping it.
- Bundle size (vite build): AgentsView 21.7 kB (6.6 gz, unchanged); AgentConfigTab 72.8 kB (20.9 gz); AgentPoliciesView 56.5 kB (18.4 gz); shared workspace chunk 101.9 kB (35.8 gz: js-yaml, validation, workspace, inline editors); ReviewSaveDialog 19.8 kB and RawOverlayDialog 5.1 kB are async; CodeMirror stays in CodeEditor 46.4 kB / CodeMergeView 29.3 kB async chunks. The drawer chunk (86.2 kB) is gone.
